### Shard 05 — Platform configuration, admin and quality > Contracts > Platform-Owned Setting Definitions
### Platform-Owned Setting Definitions

This shard governs settings, so its own numeric bounds are registered setting definitions rather than prose. Every key below is a `SettingDefinitionVersion` created by a code/contract release under CFG-01 — never minted by an admin — and is resolved through CFG-02 like any other value. The **launch seed is normative**: an unreadable, absent or out-of-schema value fails closed to the seed rather than to "no limit". No value may exceed its ceiling, and `risk_class` fixes who may change it.

| Setting key | Value kind | Seed value | Ceiling | Risk class | Guarded by | Applies to |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `admin.search.min_count_suppression_threshold` | `integer` | 5 — an aggregate, facet or total resolving to fewer than 5 authorized items is suppressed rather than returned | 25 | `high` | `COUNT_SUPPRESSED` | CFG-09 |
| `admin.search.count_bucket_size` | `integer` | 10 — counts at or above the threshold are reported to the nearest lower multiple of 10, never exactly | 100 | `high` | — | CFG-09 |
| `admin.search.max_page_size` | `integer` | 100 cursor-bounded results per page | 500 | `medium` | `VALIDATION_FAILED` | CFG-09 |
| `admin.bulk.max_batch_size` | `integer` | 5000 frozen targets per manifest | 20000 | `high` | `BATCH_TOO_LARGE` | CFG-10 |
| `admin.notification.max_attempts` | `integer` | 5 delivery attempts per dispatch, under the platform backoff | 10 | `medium` | `NOTICE_UNDELIVERABLE` | CFG-15 |
| `admin.notification.dedupe_window_minutes` | `integer` | 15 minutes per (source, recipient, channel) | 60 | `medium` | — | CFG-15 |
| `config.kill_switch.step_up_freshness` | `duration` | 5 minutes since the incident operator's last successful step-up | 15 minutes | `emergency` | `STEP_UP_REQUIRED` | CFG-07 |
| `config.approval.mfa_freshness` | `duration` | 15 minutes since an approver's last successful MFA | 60 minutes | `high` | `STEP_UP_REQUIRED` | CFG-04, CFG-11 |
| `config.diagnostic.default_timeout_ms` | `integer` | 5000 ms, overridden per definition by `DiagnosticDefinitionVersion.timeout_ms` | 30000 | `medium` | `DIAGNOSTIC_TIMEOUT` | CFG-12 |
| `quality.export.default_expiry_hours` | `integer` | 72 hours from `ready` | 168 | `high` | — | CFG-13 |

`admin.search.min_count_suppression_threshold` and `admin.search.count_bucket_size` together define the "minimum-count policy" CFG-09 refers to: below the threshold the count is suppressed entirely and the response says so; at or above it the count is bucketed downward to the nearest multiple of the bucket size. A count is **never** returned exactly, because an exact count differenced across two capability scopes is itself a side channel. Both keys carry `risk_class = high`, so no ordinary admin can lower them.

