### Shard 04 — CMS navigation, media and delivery > Contracts > Navigation, Route, and Discovery
### Navigation, Route, and Discovery

| Contract | Locked rule |
|---|---|
| Named locations | Launch locations: `primary, utility, footer, legal, account`; code/design system owns location contract; CMS binds one active version per locale/audience class. |
| Menu limits | Protected defaults: maximum depth 3, 200 items/tree, 50 siblings; complete-tree publish only; keyboard-equivalent ordering required. |
| Target kinds | Active content publication, approved internal route, or allowlisted HTTPS external URL. No `javascript:`, data URL, open redirect, preview/admin/private target. |
| Visibility vocabulary | `always, anonymous, authenticated, locale, capability, entitlement, feature_available` with AND over bounded predicates; no arbitrary expressions or sensitive client-derived conditions. |
| Reserved routes | `/api, /admin, /auth, /_astro, /.well-known, /health, /preview` and code-declared prefixes cannot be CMS slugs. |
| Slug/redirect | Unicode NFC, lowercase locale rules, slash-delimited safe segments; one canonical route; permanent redirect history; maximum five hops; cycles/collisions reject. |
| Discovery override | Privacy, unclaimed/suppressed party, embargo, legal/safety, authorization, archive/unpublish and noindex policy override all editorial SEO/social/sitemap settings. |
| Authoring commands | Four protected commands write this section's state: `SaveMenuDraft` (navigation editor — DLV-01), `PublishMenuVersion` (CMS publisher — DLV-02), `SetCanonicalSlug` (navigation editor — DLV-03) and `SaveDiscoveryMetadata` (navigation editor — DLV-04). Each carries the caller's capability and an idempotency key. An expected version is carried only where the subject declares one and the command edits it: `PublishMenuVersion` names the expected currently-active `MenuVersion` for that (`menu_id`, `locale`, `audience_class`), and `SaveMenuDraft` names the expected `MenuVersion` version of the draft it edits — a first draft has no prior version to name. `SetCanonicalSlug` carries none, because it compiles a new immutable `RouteManifestVersion` and competing path claims serialize on the (`manifest_id`, `normalized_path`, `locale`) uniqueness constraint; `SaveDiscoveryMetadata` carries none, because `DiscoveryMetadataVersion` declares no `version` field and its writes serialize on the (`publication_id`, `locale`) uniqueness constraint. No editor command activates anything: `SaveMenuDraft` rests at `MenuVersion.state = draft`, `SetCanonicalSlug` rests at `RouteManifestVersion.state = ready`, and only `PublishMenuVersion` flips an active pointer. |

### Shard 00 — Cross-cutting platform foundation > Edge Cases
## Edge Cases

| Case | Required result |
|---|---|
| Expired/revoked session during command | Reject before mutation; preserve unsent client input locally; return reauthentication path. |
| Valid user supplies another party/resource ID | Deny under server capability check and RLS; emit sanitized security telemetry. |
| Same idempotency key, different body | Return 409; do not execute or replace the original result. |
| Stale `If-Match` | Return 409 with sanitized current-version guidance; no partial effects. |
| Database commits but client disconnects | Retry with the same idempotency key returns the committed result/status. |
| Outbox dispatch repeats | Consumer deduplicates and re-reads current aggregate/version; effect occurs once. |
| Queue eve…

…otion; old code remains compatible; no destructive rollback migration. |
| New route/consumer lacks SLO registration | CI fails before artifact promotion. |
| Logging receives forbidden field | Observability package redacts/drops it and raises a test/diagnostic signal. |
| Forged acting-party ID or user-editable JWT role | Ignore supplied authority, resolve server-side, deny mismatch, and record sanitized abuse telemetry. |
| Webhook signature is valid but timestamp is outside `infra.webhook.replay_window` (seed 300 seconds) | Reject without trusted receipt/work; return the same generic `INVALID_REQUEST` used for an invalid signature so no signature or clock oracle is exposed. |
| Queue env…

…quests an older/unknown schema version | Known stale versions are handled idempotently; unknown versions dead-letter without execution. |
| Object key contains traversal/control characters | Reject before signing; keys are server-generated, normalized, and never derived directly from filenames. |
| User input attempts newline/log-field injection | Structured logger encodes values, applies the denylist, and prevents caller replacement of reserved identifiers. |
| PITR missing or older than required window | Disable protected production writes for money/rights/publication and escalate via runbook. |
| Scheduled maintenance | Announc…

### Shard 03 — CMS content modeling and authoring > Contracts > Field Kind Constraint Schemas
### Field Kind Constraint Schemas

`field_kind` is a **closed set of exactly 14 members**. It is the domain of `FieldDefinitionVersion.kind` and is declared once, here. Each kind admits exactly the `constraints` keys listed for it; an unrecognised key is rejected at compile, not ignored, and a key valid for another kind is equally rejected.

| `field_kind` member | Permitted `constraints` keys | Payload shape in `EntryFieldValue` |
|---|---|---|
| `short_text` | `min_length` (integer ≥ 0), `max_length` (integer, 1–512, default 255), `pattern` (RE2 source string), `trim` (boolean) | JSON string |
| `long_text` | `min_length` (integer ≥ 0), `max_length` (integer, 1–65536, default 20000) | JSON string |
| `rich_text` | `allowed_node_types` (non-empty array from the approved structured-AST node registry), `max_nodes` (integer, 1–10000, default 5000), `allow_embeds` (boolean) | Approved structured AST object, **never raw executable HTML** |
| `boolean` | none | JSON `true` or `false` |
| `integer` | `min` (integer), `max` (integer), `step` (integer > 0) | JSON integer |
| `decimal` | `min` (decimal), `max` (decimal), `precision` (integer, 1–38), `scale` (integer, 0–`precision`) | JSON string carrying an exact decimal; never a float |
| `date` | `min` (ISO 8601 date), `max` (ISO 8601 date) | ISO 8601 date string |
| `datetime` | `min` / `max` (RFC 3339 instant), `require_timezone` (boolean, default `true`) | RFC 3339 instant string |
| `enum` | `values` (non-empty array of stable member keys, unique, immutable once activated), `multiple` (boolean) | Member key, or array of member keys when `multiple` |
| `taxonomy` | `vocabulary_key` (must resolve to a `TaxonomyVersion` this type is allowed to use), `max_terms` (integer, 1–50, default 10), `require_leaf` (boolean) | Array of `Term` IDs, materialized as `TermAssignment` rows |
| `relation` | governed entirely by the field's `RelationDefinition` row — `target_kind`, `cardinality`, `allowed_projection`, `on_unavailable`. No other key is permitted on the field itself. | Array of target UUIDs, materialized as `EntryRelation` rows |
| `media` | `allowed_media_types` (non-empty array of Shard 04 media kinds), `max_items` (integer, 1–50, default 1), `require_alt_text` (boolean, default `true`) | Array of Shard 04 media asset IDs |
| `object` | `properties` (map of member key → nested field-kind definition, recursively constrained by this same table), `required_properties` (array of member keys) | JSON object keyed by member key |
| `list` | `item` (a single nested field-kind definition, recursively constrained by this same table), `min_items` (integer ≥ 0), `max_items` (integer, 1–500, default 100) | JSON array |

`object` and `list` may nest to `cms.field.max_nest_depth`; `relation` may not appear inside `object` or `list`, because a relation's authority recheck is per-row and cannot be expressed inside a JSONB subtree.

