### Shard 36 — Door access, box office, reconciliation and ticketing risk > Access Control
…ss Control

| Actor | Allowed | Denied |
|---|---|---|
| Fan/holder/payer | Own ticket/change/refund/transfer/exchange/consent states | Other attendees, counts, fraud signals |
| Door staff | Provisioned scanner, scan/name lookup, age result and ordinary override | Sales/refunds/count certification/PII export |
| Box-office seller | Walk-up sales/float and own device reconciliation | Scan-only role assumptions or settlement edits |
| Operator/box-office lead | Device provisioning, close/certify, external mapping and exception approval | Fan marketing without consent |
| Performing act | Minimum count aggregates/drops and counter-attestation | Fan rows, device PII, unrelated money |
| Finance/refund role | Obligations/provider reconcile/alternative incident | Door lookup/marketing use |
| Fraud/moderation role | Circumvention/resale/dispute evidence under case scope | Automatic hidden block or broad attendee export |
| Named event party | Consented attendee export/use for exact purpose | Transactional data or other party's consents |
| Service principal (ingestion/projection) | **Exactly three write paths, each bounded to the projection it maintains and to nothing else.** (a) 36.03 — reconcile co-located scanner replicas on the peer interval, writing duplicate and conflict detections with causal order confidence onto the scan log. (b) 36.08 — run the pacing evaluation on its interval, writing a deviation alert or silence…

…can verdict (36.02, 36.04), sell (36.09), refund, cancel, transfer, or bind an external mapping.** It may not auto-bind or auto-convert a mapping an operator has not confirmed, may not emit a pacing claim where no reference exists, and derives no authority from an event it consumed. It reads no fan PII beyond the token and name-lookup fields the device replica already carries. |
| Support operator | Mechanical recovery on a **single named object** under an expiring purpose grant: re-drive a stuck refund-obligation provider call, re-issue a device provisioning epoch, replay a failed external ingestion batch, restore a scanner repl…

…l, certify a close or choose a reconciliation number; read attendee rows, fraud signals, consent payloads or age-verification outcomes; or act outside the single object the grant names. A support grant is recovery of an object and is never acquisition of authority. |

- Device replica includes only fields needed for token/name lookup and age flag; encrypted at rest.
- Age verification stores outcome/reason class, never ID image/number.
- Consent withdrawal propagates platform suppression and recipient notification/audit; off-platform deletion cannot be falsely guaranteed.

### Shard 37 — Fanbase and direct-to-fan > Access Control
## Access Control

| Actor | Allowed | Explicitly denied |
|---|---|---|
| Fan | Manage own consent/preferences/follows, library, memberships, orders and requests | See another fan's relationship, score, purchases, location or consent |
| Browser-local visitor | Create/remove local follows and browse public stores | Receive alerts, create durable relationship or access private library |
| Artist entity actor | Manage own store, tiers, vault, segments and gated campaigns under mandate | Grant consent, identify followers, inspect cross-artist behavior, bypass suppression |
| Collaborator | Approve publication/rights facts where separately authorized | Gain audience/store authority from collaboration alone |
| Operator/venue | Consume only explicit event/ticket aggregates from owned shows | Run artist memberships, sell artist merch or inspect fan demand at consumer launch |
| Trust & Safety | Moderate messages/content and preserve evidence under scoped case | Read campaign audience or commerce data without case purpose |
| Support | Resolve disclosed order/delivery cases through audited support grants | Restore consent, reveal affinity factors broadly or override permanent entitlement |
| Platform administrator | Configure versioned policy and disable capabilities | Impersonate fan consent, export raw audience or activate counsel-gated features alone |
| Service principal | Execute one declared contract with least-privilege schema access | Join PII, commerce and cross-artist analytics outside approved projection |

RLS keys every entity-managed record by entity and mandate. Sensitive reads require purpose-bound audit context. Controller-change, bulk export, campaign activation and permanent policy changes require step-up authentication; controller-change and gated-feature activation also require dual control. Enterprise SSO and enterprise administration remain deferred.

### Shard 27 — Digital catalog, entitlement, delivery and vendor QA > Accessibility
## Accessibility

- Type-conditional forms announce required sections and preserve draft progress when schema changes.
- Compatibility/dependency verdicts separate unsupported, unknown and known-issue in text; no color-only badge.
- Audio auditions/downloads provide keyboard controls, captions/descriptions, duration, size and format before action.
- Transfer progress states bytes served, estimated finish, expiry and queue position; percentage is supplemental.
- Library tables expose holder, entitlement, vendor and management state as separate labeled fields.
- Terms diffs are clause-by-clause, readable without side-by-side color and focus the first changed obligation.
- QA/review errors link to exact artifact/check and remain exportable for vendor remediation.

